# Chaos: additive spell effects (O233; client/BASE.md "69zs"; src/client/chaosglow.h (new, pure), map.h, tile.cpp, mapview.cpp,
# luafunctions_client.cpp, src/framework/graphics/painter.h/.cpp, drawqueue.h/.cpp; after 0001-0150).
# Magic effects (Effect, not missiles or creatures) of a bright theme are drawn added onto what is under them, so fire, energy,
# holy and arcane hits brighten the map instead of covering it. Which ids: the Lua list L.glowIds() of game_visualfx
# (visualfx_logic.lua, unit tested), sent once with g_map.addGlowEffect; smoke, blood, poison, water, frost, shadow, earth,
# healing, combat feedback and every effect of no theme keep the normal blend.
#  * Painter::CompositionMode_AddAlpha: glBlendFuncSeparate(GL_SRC_ALPHA, GL_ONE, GL_ZERO, GL_ONE), dst + src * alpha; the
#    framebuffer alpha is kept, so the map picture's alpha does not fill up and soft sprite edges add little.
#  * DrawQueueConditionGlow / DrawQueue::setGlow(start): the items queued since start are drawn inside that blend. A draw queue
#    condition already makes DrawQueue::draw flush the draw cache before its start and before its end, so the range is one batch
#    between two blend changes. The atlas bind inside the cache saves and restores the painter state (FrameBuffer::bind/release),
#    so a sprite that enters the atlas in the middle of the range does not drop the blend.
#  * Batching: Tile::drawTop does not queue a listed effect, it hands it to Map::deferGlowEffect (id, dest and offsets kept, at
#    most 64 per floor; the 65th and later draw normal). MapView::drawFloor ends with one range: all held effects of the floor
#    are queued after the missiles and setGlow wraps them. So a floor with glowing effects costs 2 cache flushes and 2 blend
#    changes however many effects play, a floor with none costs nothing, and a frame with the usual one floor costs 2 and 2.
#    Deferral is only on while drawFloor runs (beginGlowFloor/endGlowFloor), so a drawTop from elsewhere draws normally.
#  * Tied to the existing option `spellLight` (no new option, no new text, the options panel is unchanged): game_visualfx calls
#    g_map.setGlowEffects(on) with it. Unlike the spell light, the glow also shows in full daylight.
#  * Lua binding: g_map.clearGlowEffects(), addGlowEffect(id), setGlowEffects(bool), isGlowEffects(). Off in the engine by
#    default, so an engine without the module draws as before.
# Cost: off, one bool test per drawn effect. On, per glowing effect the same textured rect as before plus one vector push; the
# additive range overdraws like any effect. Not measured on a GPU.
# Checked: applies after 0001-0150 on the base client tree (no fuzz); the touched .cpp files pass g++ -fsyntax-only; the header
# passes client/tools/chaosglow_test.cpp. Not built, linked or run in a client.
